  "seoTitle": "Landslides Hit Multiple South Jakarta Locations",
  "metaDescription": "Heavy rainfall causes multiple landslides across West and Central Java, damaging homes and infrastructure while emergency teams work on evacuations.",
  "aiSummaryBullets": [
    "Emergency response teams in Banjarnegara successfully evacuated four survivors from a recent landslide site.",
    "Multiple districts in Tasikmalaya and Purwakarta report significant damage to housing and infrastructure following landslides.",
    "Authorities in South Jakarta and Trenggalek are prioritizing construction of permanent retaining walls and clearing debris from blocked roads."
  ],
  "aiContextParagraph": "Recent heavy rainfall has triggered widespread landslides across multiple regions in West and Central Java. The incidents have caused significant disruption, with reports of damage to numerous residential properties in Tasikmalaya, where 17 districts have been affected. In Pejaten Timur, South Jakarta, local government authorities have accelerated the construction of permanent concrete retaining walls to mitigate flood and landslide risks after repeat incidents. Meanwhile, in Banjarnegara, disaster management agencies and volunteers have conducted successful evacuation operations for survivors. Other locations, including Purwakarta, Temanggung, and the Southern Cross Road in Trenggalek, are facing challenges with landslide damage and accessibility issues for travelers. Rescue efforts in areas like the Pongkor mine continue to be complicated by the persistent threat of subsequent landslides due to ongoing severe weather conditions throughout the affected provinces.",
